\end{xltabular}

\subsection{Test stratification rules}

\normsv{} The following discipline applies to every case above:

\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=2em,itemsep=0.15em]
    \item \textbf{All three layers must pass.} A green L1 with
    a missing L2 or L3 \textbf{is not} a pass; report it as a
    fail with the missing layer named.
    \item \textbf{Failures print evidence from each layer.}
    Stderr (L1) + response body or trace (L2) + DB row /
    receipt entry / FS state (L3). No bare ``FAIL''.
    \item \textbf{The harness keeps the environment alive on
    fail.} \texttt{KEEP\_DOCKER\_E2E=1} is the default for
    debugging; the harness does not tear down on first fail.
    \item \textbf{e2e cases run in docker with two hubs (Phase
    2+).} The cross-hub topology from
    \texttt{docker/e2e/docker-compose-cross-hub.yml} is the
    minimum for Phase 2 e2e cases.
    \item \textbf{Receipts are queried, not synthesised.} L3
    checks query the receipt store the daemon actually wrote
    to; tests \textbf{must not} construct a fake receipt to
    satisfy a check.
\end{itemize}

